    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1409" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aeternālis</span></b> , e, adj.
		aeternus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>enduring forever</i>, <i>everlasting</i> (often in inscrr.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aeternali somno sacrum,</span>”
				i. e. <i>to death</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Grut. 752, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">domus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 4518</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">luctus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib. 4604</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">memoria,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib. 200</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lex temporalis et aeternalis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Jud. 6</span></i>
			.—<i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aeternālĭter</span></b> , <i>forever</i> (late Lat.), Ad. ad H.
					<i><span class="en">Prud. March, p. 245</span></i>.</div>
